      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Part of # 3 6 6 9 2. This replaces the field-by-field construction of transaction inputs and outputs in `multisig_tests` with `COutPoint`, `CTxIn` and `CTxOut` constructor calls.\r\n\r\nIt keeps `CMutableTransaction` as the builder, since a `CTransaction` constructor taking inputs and outputs directly is still under discussion (# 3 6 6 9 6). If one is added, the `vin`/`vout` lists here can be passed to it directly.\r\n\r\nThis change is test-only and does not change the constructed transactions:\r\n\r\n- The funding outputs were previously created by `vout.resize(3)` and only had their `scriptPubKey` assigned, leaving `nValue` at its null value (`-1`). The `-1` is now spelled out explicitly, which makes this previously hidden value visible.\r\n- The loop index is changed from `int` to `uint32_t` to match `COutPoint::n`, as brace-initialization does not allow the narrowing conversion.\r\n\r\nTo check that the transactions are identical, I temporarily built the old and new versions side by side in the same test run and compared them. Their txids and wtxids matched in both `multisig_verify` and `multisig_Sign`.",
